# ask — the first conversation over an edge (card:edge.md, 2026-09-02, at Henri's "aloita
# connect-mittauksesta"): pull the llm, wait for it to answer, ask it one thing, say the answer into
# this state, let go.  `pull llm` is the signal — the edge the process holds — and `connect 18080` is
# the talk: keep lets the program reach that one port and nothing else.  The question is `run`'s
# arguments, or one about the tree when there are none.  The llm's own sitting and idle are its own
allow ask.py
pull llm
connect 18080
program /usr/bin/python3 $NODE/ask.py
